  "full_prompt": "Create an animation explaining Taylor series. Start with higher order derivatives: show second derivative as rate of change of slope (curvature), with positive second derivative meaning concave up and negative meaning concave down. Use the analogy of position, velocity, acceleration, jerk for derivatives. Then show Taylor polynomials: approximate a function near a point by matching derivatives at that point. For f(x) = cos(x), show the constant term (matches value), linear term (matches first derivative), quadratic term (matches second derivative), etc. Demonstrate how adding more terms improves the approximation. Explain that the Taylor series is the infinite sum, with factorial denominators coming from repeated differentiation of power terms. Show examples of convergence (e^x) and divergence (ln(x) beyond radius of convergence).",
